            ]
          },
          "worked": "Both $p$ and $q$ belong to $\\{1,2,3,4\\}$. The possible ratios, grouped by denominator, are:\n\nFor $q=1$: $1,2,3,4$.\n\nFor $q=2$: $\\frac12,1,\\frac32,2$.\n\nFor $q=3$: $\\frac13,\\frac23,1,\\frac43$.\n\nFor $q=4$: $\\frac14,\\frac12,\\frac34,1$.\n\nRemove repeated values:\n$$X=\\left\\{\\frac14,\\frac13,\\frac12,\\frac23,\\frac34,1,\\frac43,\\frac32,2,3,4\\right\\}.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p46-q69-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "By changing two symbols only, a new set $Y$ can be made that represents all positive real numbers. Which two symbols need to be changed?",
