              {
                "id": "p46-q69-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Allow real numerators and denominators; their ratios cover every positive real number.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Replace $\\mathbb Q$ and $\\mathbb Z$ by $\\mathbb R$:\n$$Y=\\left\\{\\frac pq\\in\\mathbb R\\text{ where }p,q\\in\\mathbb R\\text{ and }p,q\\in(0,4]\\right\\}.$$\nEvery allowed ratio is positive. To obtain any positive real number $r$:\n\nIf $r\\ge1$, choose $p=4$ and $q=\\frac{4}{r}$. Both lie in $(0,4]$, and\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac pq&=\\frac{4}{\\frac{4}{r}}\\\\\\frac pq&=r.\\end{align*}$$\nIf $0<r<1$, choose $p=4r$ and $q=4$. Both lie in $(0,4]$, and\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac pq&=\\frac{4r}{4}\\\\\\frac pq&=r.\\end{align*}$$\nThus the new set contains exactly all positive real numbers.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
